2026-09-27T03:27:30.3445554Z Description:
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3446055Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3446632Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3447684Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3448881Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3449014Z Update Note
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3449329Z ===========
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3449753Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3450146Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3450280Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3450602Z ================
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3450808Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3451028Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3451588Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3451923Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3452105Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3452498Z ====================================
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3452771Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3452993Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3453597Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3454133Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3455206Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3456109Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3456277Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3457229Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3458082Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3458512Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3458977Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3459605Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3459745Z Packages
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3460018Z ========
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3460189Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3462282Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3464395Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3464741Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3465506Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3466273Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3467363Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3468284Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3468946Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3469371Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3469971Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3470362Z ==========================
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3470618Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3472427Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3474601Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3475683Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3477323Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T03:27:30.3477698Z 
